{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-78233" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the equation of the hyperbola $5{x}^{2}-6{y}^{2}=60$ in standard form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013795/state.json" "file_sha256" "f753ce88c6d176374b9559221b259966576926f20420bccc045d3c360a3bbe63"} {"question" "q-78233" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Cartesian equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $60$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-6{y}^{2} & =60 \\\\ \\frac{5{x}^{2}}{60}-\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{60} & =\\frac{60}{60} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{10} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013795/state.json" "file_sha256" "f753ce88c6d176374b9559221b259966576926f20420bccc045d3c360a3bbe63"} {"question" "q-78233" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013795/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76a2ba6071e33b52a090a679f7b989389e57ebf7b0c3a22b206bdf1fdcb53857"} {"question" "q-78233" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013795/state.json" "file_sha256" "f753ce88c6d176374b9559221b259966576926f20420bccc045d3c360a3bbe63"} {"question" "q-78233" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{10}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{15}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013795/state.json" "file_sha256" "f753ce88c6d176374b9559221b259966576926f20420bccc045d3c360a3bbe63"} {"question" "q-78233" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{10}=1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013795/state.json" "file_sha256" "f753ce88c6d176374b9559221b259966576926f20420bccc045d3c360a3bbe63"} {"question" "q-78234" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the equation of the hyperbola $3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=18$ in standard form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013795/state.json" "file_sha256" "f753ce88c6d176374b9559221b259966576926f20420bccc045d3c360a3bbe63"} {"question" "q-78234" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Cartesian equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $18$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{18}-\\frac{2{y}^{2}}{18} & =\\frac{18}{18} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013795/state.json" "file_sha256" "f753ce88c6d176374b9559221b259966576926f20420bccc045d3c360a3bbe63"} {"question" "q-78234" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jak